# The Last Ember: a story written in Looped Script.
#
# This file is the story itself: its title, the files that hold the rest,
# where you start, the numbers it keeps, the things you can carry, and the
# light you carry once you have the lantern. The places and what happens in
# them are in the files it reads, one place a file.

story The Last Ember
  by: J Production
  words from words.looped
  read colours.looped, things.looped, people.looped
  read village.looped, woods.looped, ford.looped, island.looped, peak.looped, hill.looped, morning.looped
  you start in the village
  keep count of embers
  keep count of kindness
  keep count of courage
  a light when you have the old lantern: a lantern flame that flickers gently

item old lantern: Mira's lantern, dented and warm. One spark still lives inside it.
item honey bread: Still warm, wrapped in a cloth. Tobin's mother baked it for whoever climbs the hill.
item silver bell: A bell no bigger than a thimble. It rings like rain on a roof.
item woods ember: A coal from the roots of the great oak. It hums like a sleeping bee.
item river ember: A coal that burns blue at its edges, cool and smooth as a stone from the ford.
item peak ember: A coal so bright it makes your eyes water. Snow melts wherever you carry it.
